  "title": "Qt: Fix crash on exit with previous focus",
  "description": "If the main window previous focus exists, disconnect the signal that\nis called when the focus is destroyed in the main window destructor,\nor else that will be called after the main window is destroyed:\n\n ** (wireshark:2115850) 12:31:24.221922 [GUI ERROR] /usr/include/qt6/QtCore/qobjectdefs_impl.h:129 -- ASSERT failure in WiresharkMainWindow: \"Called object is not of the correct type (class destructor may have already run)\", file /usr/include/qt6/QtCore/qobjectdefs_impl.h, line 129\n ** (wireshark:2115850) Aborting on fatal log level exception\n\nThis somehow happens with the new-style signals and slots, but not the\nold ones.\n\nFollow up to !16014",
